WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.755 --> 00:00:15.036
Julia had no idea what was happening.

2
00:00:16.036 --> 00:00:18.497
She couldn't hear anything but the rush of air around her.

3
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:24.058
Then she landed on a hard marble floor.

4
00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:27.259
She stumbled forward, letting go of Brody's arm.

5
00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:29.660
"What's going on?"

6
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.840
Brody shouted.

7
00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:35.926
"Hey!" Julia looked around, too frightened to speak.

8
00:00:37.688 --> 00:00:40.029
They were in a square room with stone walls.

9
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:44.312
A skylight overhead let in a beam of bright sunshine.

10
00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:49.816
Two young men stood in front of them.

11
00:00:50.556 --> 00:00:54.019
Both were tall and handsome and dressed in short robes.

12
00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:57.421
"Chitons," Julia thought.

13
00:00:58.962 --> 00:01:01.664
She remembered learning that word in social studies class.

14
00:01:02.724 --> 00:01:07.048
Chitons were simple garments worn by men and women in the ancient world.

15
00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:14.015
The classes about ancient Greece and Rome had been among Julia's favorite parts of social studies last year.

16
00:01:15.016 --> 00:01:16.738
But why were these guys wearing chitons?

17
00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:19.160
What had happened to the high school?

18
00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:22.263
"Where did the girl come from?"

19
00:01:22.884 --> 00:01:23.685
one guy asked.

20
00:01:23.705 --> 00:01:26.708
"She wasn't part of the plan."

21
00:01:29.096 --> 00:01:34.178
The young man's face was so beautiful that it took Julia a moment to notice something odd.

22
00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:39.080
He had only a single lock of brown hair hanging over his forehead.

23
00:01:40.121 --> 00:01:42.041
The rest of his head was completely bald.

24
00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:47.584
The second young man had curly blond hair and was as handsome as a movie star.

25
00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:52.226
He leaned forward and poked Julia.

26
00:01:52.246 --> 00:01:54.266
"You, girl," he said.

27
00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:55.927
"What are you doing here?"

28
00:01:57.248 --> 00:01:59.584
"Ow!" Julia yanked her arm away.

29
00:01:59.604 --> 00:02:01.405
"Stop poking me."

30
00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:03.626
"What's going on?"

31
00:02:04.106 --> 00:02:05.246
Brody demanded again.

32
00:02:05.266 --> 00:02:07.087
"Where are we?"

33
00:02:07.107 --> 00:02:09.867
"Silence, mortal."

34
00:02:10.207 --> 00:02:12.148
The blond man frowned at his friend.

35
00:02:12.168 --> 00:02:15.109
"The girl was a mistake.

36
00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:16.569
Let's toss her back through."

37
00:02:16.589 --> 00:02:19.470
"Are you certain you want to do that?"

38
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.910
the bald guy said.

39
00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:26.612
"Remember, this passage will close forever as soon as anyone passes back through it."

40
00:02:29.224 --> 00:02:30.065
"I forgot about that."

41
00:02:30.445 --> 00:02:31.926
The blond guy looked annoyed.

42
00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:34.647
"In that case, she'll have to stay.

43
00:02:35.068 --> 00:02:37.189
We might need the passage again if this doesn't work out."

44
00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:41.231
He glanced at Brody and looked him up and down.

45
00:02:41.251 --> 00:02:44.593
"Are we being kidnapped?"

46
00:02:45.053 --> 00:02:48.395
Julia blurted out, still trying to figure out what was happening.

47
00:02:48.415 --> 00:02:49.936
"Who are you?"

48
00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.737
The blond guy chuckled.

49
00:02:51.757 --> 00:02:55.299
"Do not be frightened, mortal.

50
00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:56.380
We won't hurt you.

51
00:02:57.984 --> 00:02:59.025
Don't you recognize me?

52
00:02:59.605 --> 00:03:02.966
I am Hermes, messenger of the gods and friend to mortals."

53
00:03:04.747 --> 00:03:06.628
"Mortals? Gods?"

54
00:03:07.308 --> 00:03:08.049
Brody said.

55
00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:12.971
"Huh?" Hermes held up a hand to silence him.

56
00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:17.573
"And this is my friend Caerus, god of luck and opportunity.

57
00:03:18.193 --> 00:03:24.196
He saw the opportunity to help me humiliate Zeus by seeking a mortal champion in an unusual way."

58
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.481
Hermes and Caerus both laughed heartily.

59
00:03:31.962 --> 00:03:34.482
Julia caught a glimpse of movement and looked down.

60
00:03:36.563 --> 00:03:40.424
Her eyes widened when she saw little golden wings on Hermes' sandals.

61
00:03:41.384 --> 00:03:42.645
They were flapping gently.

62
00:03:43.445 --> 00:03:51.107
Could it be "I do have some influence over time and seasons," Caerus said, puffing out his chest

63
00:03:51.187 --> 00:03:57.005
proudly. "Not that Zeus would ever notice—he treats me like a demigod.

64
00:03:58.827 --> 00:04:02.550
He'll never figure out that I helped Hermes defeat him with a champion from the future."

65
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:07.194
"What? This is stupid," Brody said loudly.

66
00:04:07.214 --> 00:04:10.156
"Look, I'm tired of your dumb stories.

67
00:04:10.577 --> 00:04:12.979
Why did you really grab me and drag me in here?"

68
00:04:12.999 --> 00:04:17.843
"It's quite simple, my simple mortal friend," Hermes said.

69
00:04:17.863 --> 00:04:21.586
"You see, the next Olympic Games will begin soon."

70
00:04:21.606 --> 00:04:23.988
"The Olympics?"

71
00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:25.377
Julia echoed.

72
00:04:26.357 --> 00:04:27.198
Caerus nodded.

73
00:04:27.218 --> 00:04:34.263
"And as usual, Zeus is already bragging about how his champion will easily defeat all others."

74
00:04:34.283 --> 00:04:37.846
"Yes." Hermes snorted.

75
00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:41.108
"He's being quite annoying.

76
00:04:42.369 --> 00:04:46.992
Just because he's king of the gods, he thinks nobody else can ever beat his hand-picked champion."

77
00:04:48.553 --> 00:04:49.854
Brody looked confused.

78
00:04:49.874 --> 00:04:52.316
"Zeus?" he muttered.

79
00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:54.477
"Wait, that sounds familiar.

80
00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.278
Is he from a video game or something?"

81
00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.341
"No way," Julia said, staring at the two men.

82
00:05:02.361 --> 00:05:04.263
"You're not real.

83
00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:05.763
None of this is real.

84
00:05:06.304 --> 00:05:07.444
Hermes is just a myth.

85
00:05:07.805 --> 00:05:11.087
So is Zeus—all the ancient Greek gods are from myths."

86
00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:13.508
"Greek gods?

87
00:05:14.228 --> 00:05:15.709
Like from social studies class?"

88
00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.390
Brody said with a snort.

89
00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.872
"Yeah, right.

90
00:05:20.456 --> 00:05:23.778
These two are probably just a couple of jerks from Southbridge High.

91
00:05:24.118 --> 00:05:26.459
They're trying to scare me before next week's game."

92
00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.440
Hermes traded a look with Caerus.

93
00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.801
"What are they blathering on about?"

94
00:05:31.821 --> 00:05:34.822
"Who cares," Caerus answered.

95
00:05:35.623 --> 00:05:36.783
He sounded bored again.

96
00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:38.804
"Let's move this along.

97
00:05:39.184 --> 00:05:39.724
I'm hungry."

98
00:05:39.744 --> 00:05:41.585
"All right."

99
00:05:42.025 --> 00:05:43.446
Hermes gestured to Brody.

100
00:05:43.466 --> 00:05:44.807
"Come, mortal.

101
00:05:45.347 --> 00:05:47.628
I've arranged for you to stay with a local family."

102
00:05:49.236 --> 00:05:50.337
He glanced at Julia.

103
00:05:50.357 --> 00:05:53.499
"I'm sure they can make room for the girl as well."

104
00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:02.845
"No." Julia's logical mind still refused to accept what Hermes and Caerus— or whatever their names might be—were

105
00:06:02.885 --> 00:06:03.346
telling her.

106
00:06:03.366 --> 00:06:07.088
"This isn't happening," she insisted.

107
00:06:07.108 --> 00:06:11.031
"We're not really in some temple in ancient Athens."

108
00:06:12.051 --> 00:06:13.432
Hermes sounded impatient.

109
00:06:13.452 --> 00:06:16.434
"Aren't you listening to a word I say, mortal girl?"

110
00:06:16.454 --> 00:06:19.644
"'Julia,'" she said.

111
00:06:19.664 --> 00:06:22.485
"That's my name, not 'mortal girl.'"

112
00:06:23.525 --> 00:06:24.706
Hermes ignored her.

113
00:06:24.726 --> 00:06:26.846
"Of course we're not in Athens.

114
00:06:27.206 --> 00:06:28.027
We're in Olympia.

115
00:06:28.647 --> 00:06:30.527
If you don't believe me, I'll prove it to you."

116
00:06:31.608 --> 00:06:32.968
He grabbed Julia's arm.

117
00:06:33.788 --> 00:06:38.130
Julia tried to shake him off, but his grip was as strong as iron.

118
00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:42.551
"Stop it," she yelled as he dragged her outside.

119
00:06:42.571 --> 00:06:48.316
"Let me go or I'll—whoa!"

120
00:06:48.376 --> 00:06:52.457
She stared in amazement at the sun-drenched scene spread out before her.

121
00:06:53.798 --> 00:06:55.658
It looked nothing like her hometown.

122
00:06:56.678 --> 00:07:01.260
It looked nothing like anywhere she'd ever seen, except in the pages of her social studies textbook.

123
00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:08.862
Large, gleaming marble buildings lined with columns dotted the landscape, along with many smaller structures.

124
00:07:10.402 --> 00:07:12.062
A mountain rose in the background.

125
00:07:13.663 --> 00:07:18.485
The only roads she could see were dirt ones, and there were no cars on them, just people

126
00:07:18.525 --> 00:07:23.329
in chitons walking or riding donkeys or driving carts pulled by oxen or horses.

127
00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:29.053
There were no power lines or billboards or tall buildings anywhere in sight.

128
00:07:30.214 --> 00:07:36.640
Julia's mind whirled with confusion as she realized what it looked like—an ancient Greek city!
